# Brussels

Brussels, the capital of Belgium, is a city known for its rich history, beautiful architecture, and vibrant culture. It is also the administrative heart of the European Union.

## Grand Place

The Grand Place is the central square of Brussels and a UNESCO World Heritage site. It is surrounded by opulent guildhalls, the city's Town Hall, and the Breadhouse.
> TIP: Visit in the evening to see the beautifully illuminated buildings.
![open1](./grand_place.jpeg)
![openFra](./brussels1.jpeg)

## Atomium

The Atomium is a landmark building in Brussels, originally constructed for Expo 58, the 1958 Brussels World's Fair. It is a model of an iron crystal magnified 165 billion times.
> Don't miss the panoramic view of Brussels from the top sphere.
![open1](./atomium.jpeg)
![openFra](./atomium2.jpeg)

## Manneken Pis

Manneken Pis is a famous bronze statue of a little boy urinating into a fountain. It is a symbol of the city's irreverent sense of humor.
> TIP: Check out the statue's different costumes, which are changed regularly.
![open1](./manneken_pis.jpeg)
![openFra](./manneken_pis2.jpeg)

